      "writtenOn": "2026-10-10T12:20:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Filebeat 8 does a checkpoint of the registry at intervals. It writes all file states to a new \u003cN\u003e.json snapshot and then truncates log.json.\n\nAfter a checkpoint, this code reads log.json again from the start. But the offsets of files that filebeat shipped before the checkpoint are not in log.json anymore, thus delete_shipped does not delete these files, and the wait goes until the timeout.\n\nFix: read active.dat to get the name of the current snapshot. Then read the snapshot first, and read log.json after it.",
      "revId": "f5f16d62353e3013ee254ce67a6a60247448b425",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
